    "acceptanceCriteria": [
      {
        "id": "AC-1",
        "text": "Under `app.staticFiles(\"/\", root, o -> o.spaFallback(true))`, `GET /app/users/7` with `Accept: text/html,application/xhtml+xml` and no such file is answered `200` with the bytes of `root/index.html`. [D-265; T27] Decision: SPA fallback requires `GET` or `HEAD` and an `Accept` header containing `text/html` case-insensitively; `*/*` alone does not qualify. [SDS 2026-10-19.naruserve.naruserve-v1-wave-6-6 SDS-AC-6]",
        "checked": true,
        "line": 572
      },
      {
        "id": "AC-2",
        "text": "No SPA fallback is served for `GET /app/users/7` with `Accept: application/json` (answered `404`), for a path whose file exists (the file is served), for a path an explicit `GET` route matches (the route answers) or for a path a WebSocket route owns. [D-265]",
        "checked": true,
        "line": 573
      },
      {
        "id": "AC-3",
        "text": "`GET /api/x`, `GET /api`, `GET /ws/chat` and `GET /ws` with `Accept: text/html` and no file are answered `404`, while `GET /apix` with `Accept: text/html` receives the SPA index, because exclusions match on segment boundaries of the full request path. [D-266; D-267; wave decision: SPA fallback exclusions] Decision: the full raw request path is compared with each exclusion prefix stripped of a trailing `/`, matching when equal or followed by `/`. [SDS 2026-10-19.naruserve.naruserve-v1-wave-6-6 SDS-AC-7]",
        "checked": true,
        "line": 574
      },
      {
        "id": "AC-4",
        "text": "After `spaExclude(\"/admin\")`, `GET /admin/x` and `GET /api/x` with `Accept: text/html` are both answered `404`, so configured prefixes are added to `/api/` and `/ws/` and never replace them. Decision: `spaExclude` adds prefixes; `/api/` and `/ws/` are always excluded. [wave decision: SPA fallback exclusions; D-267]",
        "checked": true,
        "line": 575
      }
    ],
