    "requirement": "The system shall, with `spaFallback(true)`, serve the mount's index file only when no file exists for the path in any mount, no explicit route matches the path and method (a `GET`/`HEAD` after a route's method mismatch falls through, as FR-STATIC-002 AC-3 decides), no WebSocket route owns the path and the `Accept` header contains `text/html`, never serve SPA fallback content under `/api/` and `/ws/`, and treat prefixes configured through `spaExclude` as additions to those two, matched on segment boundaries of the full request path.",
    "rationale": "Covers D-265, D-266 and D-267 (exclusion configuration) with the wave decision \"SPA fallback exclusions\" (W2-009; D-266, D-267). Builds on FR-HTTP-022 (fallback point) and FR-STATIC-002 (SPA content does not count as \"served by a static mount\" for `405`). Rejected alternative: letting `spaExclude` replace the defaults; an app could then expose SPA HTML at `/api/typo`, which D-266 forbids.",
